   "file": "src/tensorlbm/free_surface_lbm_2d.py",
   "marking": "604-614 (cell_conversion_threshold / force_threshold)",
   "excess_distribution": "617-626 (uniform 1/n_recv split)",
   "mass_exchange": "345-370 (Koerner eq.9 / Thuerey table 4.1)"
  },
  "decision": "Transplant the OSS selector (fill_offset = 3e-3 + the NO_IFACE_NEIGH / NO_FLUID_NEIGH demotion guard + the normal-weighted excess split) into TensorLBM's D2Q9 free-surface step, or keep the repo's Koerner/Thuerey selector?",
  "alternatives": {
   "A_repo_selector": "kappa = 1e-2, kappa_f = 0.1, uniform 1/n_recv excess split (repo status quo)",
   "B_oss_selector": "fill_offset = 3e-3, lonely = 0.1, unconditional no-iface/no-fluid demotion, eta-weighted excess split",
   "C_hybrid": "repo excess split, OSS conversion tolerances (kappa -> 3e-3).  Reachable through the existing public API (cell_conversion_threshold), so it is the only transplant that needs no library change."
  },
  "hypothesis": [
   "H1 the selector is second order for the collapse front: the A-vs-C front-curve gap |Z_A - Z_C| stays inside the 15 % owner band at every sampled T over the whole T in [0.5, 4] window, at a = 16, 32 and 48",
   "H2 the selector is first order for mass book-keeping: the OSS guard set changes the liquid-inventory drift by more than 1 % (relative)",
   "H3 the decision disagreement on identical states is dominated by the unconditional no-iface/no-fluid demotion, not by the 3.3x tolerance ratio (2x2 factorial attribution)"
  ],
  "thresholds": {
   "owner_precision_pct": 15.0,
   "arm_arm_pct": 15.0,
   "inventory_drift_pct": 1.0,
   "selector_disagreement_pct": 5.0,
   "zero_tol_mass": 1e-12
  },
  "case": {
   "name": "2D dam-break, walled box",
